 "body": {
  "available": true,
  "basis": {
   "calculation": "Value = the sum, over the remaining weeks the player is NFL-eligible, of his projection minus the replacement level at his position that week, counting a week at or below replacement as 0. Replacement is the best available free agent's projection at the position that week; when no free agent there is projected, it is the first player beyond the league's starters at the position (flex slots counted for the position that fills them in each team's best projected lineup). A week with no projection, or with no measurable replacement level, makes the value unavailable; it is never counted as 0. Each week's addition is rounded so the weeks add up exactly to the value shown.",
   "calculation_version": "tv-2",
   "comparable_within": "Values are comparable only with each other on this board: the same league and scoring, the same projections, the same remaining weeks and the same replacement rule. Values across positions compare points above each position's replacement. They are not comparable with another league, another projection source or a value from another week.",
   "cross_position": "Values across positions compare points above each position's replacement.",
   "flex_note": "League starter counts include flexible slots (FLEX, RB/WR, WR/TE, OP/superflex): each one is counted once, for the position of the player who fills it in each team's optimal projected lineup, averaged over the remaining weeks. Flex demand is dynamic: it moves with projections, byes, injuries and roster changes, so these counts are a current reference, not a fixed rule.",
   "incomplete_team_weeks": 0,
   "kdst": "Kickers and D/STs are valued like every position, against the best available free agent each week; the trade analyzer's weekly streaming lineup baseline is not part of this value.",
